Sval: ask for the default browser through NSWorkspace from macOS 12

macOS 12 deprecates LSSetDefaultHandlerForURLScheme and
LSSetDefaultRoleHandlerForContentType for NSWorkspace's
setDefaultApplicationAtURL, under which the user confirms the change. On
macOS 26 one of the deprecated calls returns an error for a change the user
accepts, so SetDefaultBrowser fails while Sval is made the default. Upstream
already uses NSWorkspace from macOS 27; the API exists from 12.

diff --git a/browser/components/shell/nsMacShellService.mm b/browser/components/shell/nsMacShellService.mm
index 6bdf108..5e945a5 100644
--- a/browser/components/shell/nsMacShellService.mm
+++ b/browser/components/shell/nsMacShellService.mm
@@ -72,11 +72,10 @@ NS_IMETHODIMP
 nsMacShellService::SetDefaultBrowser(bool aForAllUsers) {
   // Note: We don't support aForAllUsers on Mac OS X.
 
-  if (@available(macOS 27.0, *)) {
-    // macOS 27 raises a separate prompt for each LSSetDefault* call below
-    // resulting in multiple default browser change confirmation prompts.
-    // The NSWorkspace API, which avoids this problem, is available on macOS
-    // 12+, but limit its use here to macOS 27+ for now to be conservative.
+  if (@available(macOS 12.0, *)) {
+    // macOS 12 deprecates the LSSetDefault* calls below for this API, which
+    // asks the user once. Those calls can return an error for a change the
+    // user accepts, and macOS 27 raises a separate prompt for each of them.
     // We only set the default application for the http URL scheme.
     // Empirically, that has been shown to set the default browser and the
     // default handler for https/http schemes and html files.
